  "worked_solution": "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+4y)|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+4y)(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(x-1)^{2}+4y(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2xy(x-1)^{2}+2{y}^{2}(x-1)^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x(x-1)^{2}+8(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}(4x+8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}-12x+8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}-6{x}^{2}+8x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(1-6+8)-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
